signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert\nL114: \nL115:   1. 【61†readwiseio】\nL116:   2. 【62†readwise-skills】\nL117: ## Repository navigation\nL118: \nL119:   *   * 【62†Code】\nL120:   * 【63†Issues2 (2)】\nL121:   * 【64†Pull requests3 (3)】\nL122:   * 【65†Actions】\nL123:   * 【66†Projects】\nL124:   * 【67†Security and quality】\nL125:   * 【68†Insights】\nL126: \nL127: More items\nL128: \nL129: 【69†Image: readwiseio†avatars.githubusercontent.com】\nL130: \nL131: 【62†readwise-skills】\nL132: \nL133: Public\nL134: \nL135:   * 【70†Notifications】You must be signed in to change notification settings\nL136:   * 【70†Fork13 (13)】\nL137:   * 【70†Star325 (325)】You must be signed in to star a repository\nL138: ## About\nL139: \nL140: Agent skills for your Readwise and Reader data, powered by the Readwise MCP server/CLI. Triage your inbox, quiz yourself on what you've read, build a personalized now-reading page, and more.\nL141: \nL142: 【71†readwise.io/mcp†readwise.io】\nL143: \nL144: ### Resources\nL145: \nL146: 【72†Readme】\nL147: \nL148: 【73†Activity】\nL149: \nL150: 【74†Custom properties】\nL151: \nL152: ### Stars\nL153: \nL154: 325 stars\nL155: \nL156: ### Watchers\nL157: \nL158: 2 watching\nL159: \nL160: ### Forks\nL161: \nL162: 【75†13 forks】\nL163: \nL164: 【76†Report repository】\nL165: \nL166: master\nL167: \nL168: 【77†Branches】【78†Tags】\nL169: \nL170: [Input: Go to file]\nL171: \nL172: Go to file\nL173: \nL174: Code\nL175: \nL176: Open more actions menu\nL177: ## Latest commit\nL178: \nL179: \nL180: \nL181: ## History\nL182: \nL183: 35 Commits\nL184: \nL185: ## Folders and files\nL186: \nL187: Name  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\nL188: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL189: 【79†.claude-plugin】  | 【79†.claude-plugin】  |    |\nL190: 【80†.github/workflows】  | 【80†.github/workflows】  |    |\nL191: 【81†clawhub/readwise-official】  | 【81†clawhub/readwise-official】  |    |\nL192: 【82†skills】  | 【82†skills】  |    |\nL193: 【83†.gitignore】  | 【83†.gitignore】  |    |\nL194: 【84†.mcp.json】  | 【84†.mcp.json】  |    |\nL195: 【85†README.md】  | 【85†README.md】  |    |\nL196: ## Repository files navigation\nL197: \nL198:   *   * 【86†README】\nL199: \nL200: More items\nL201: ## Installation\nL202: \nL203: Prerequisite: first, make sure you have the Readwise 【71†MCP server†readwise.io】 or 【87†CLI】 installed (whichever you prefer!)\nL204: If you're using an AI agent, you can probably just tell your agent to install the skills from this repo and let it do the work:\nL205: \nL206:     `Install the skills from here https://github.com/readwiseio/readwise-skills so that you can use them. If neither is installed yet, the Readwise MCP server is a remote MCP server hosted at https://mcp2.readwise.io/mcp OR the CLI can be installed via `npm i @readwise/cli`. You only need one of these installed to use the skills.\nL207:     `\nL208: \nL209: If that doesn't work:\nL210: ### npx skills (recommended)\nL211: \nL212: `npx skills` is a very easy way to install these skills; it will set them to work with any LLM app you might use (Claude, Codex, Opencode, Cursor, etc). Run this from the terminal:\nL213: \nL214:     `npx skills add readwiseio/readwise-skills\nL215:     `\nL216: \nL217: ### Manual Installation\nL218: \nL219: Copy the `skills/` directory into your agent's skills path:\nL220: \nL221:   * Claude Code: `~/.claude/skills/` or `.claude/skills/` in your project\nL222:   * Codex CLI: `~/.codex/skills/`\nL223:   * OpenCode: `~/.opencode/skills/`\nL224: ### Claude Code Installation (with MCP Included)\nL225: \nL226: Installs the MCP server and all skills in one command:\nL227: \nL228:     `/plugin marketplace add readwiseio/readwise-skills\nL229:     /plugin install readwise@readwise-skills\nL230:     `\nL231: \nL232: ### Claude Cowork Installation (with MCP Included)\nL233: \nL234: In the Cowork sidebar: Customize → \"+\" → Add marketplace from GitHub → enter `readwiseio/readwise-skills`. Then browse and install the Readwise plugin.\nL235: ## The Skills\nL236: \nL237: We've started this repo off with a few skills we've really enjoyed using, but so much more is possible!\nL238: Skill  | Description\nL239: --- | ---\nL240: 【88†readwise-cli】  | Teaches your agent how to use the Readwise CLI — command syntax, setup, and common workflows\nL241: 【89†readwise-mcp】  | Teaches your agent how to use the Readwise MCP tools — tool names, parameters, and common workflows\nL242: 【90†triage】  | AI walks you through your inbox one article at a time, telling you what's worth your time and why\nL243: 【91†feed-catchup】  | Skim your Reader feed in batches — RSS, newsletters, Twitter digests — pull out the gems, mark the rest as seen\nL244: 【92†quiz】  | Test yourself on something you just read — graded like a smart colleague who also read the piece\nL245: 【93†book-review】  | Draft a long-form book review from your highlights — synthesizing the book with your broader reading history\nL246: 【94†reader-recap】  | Conversational briefing on your recent reading — what you finished, highlighted, and had to say about it\nL247: 【95†surprise-me】  | Analyze your reading history and tell you something surprising you don't know about yourself\nL248: 【96†highlight-graph】  | Visualize your highlights as an interactive 2D graph showing connections between ideas across sources\nL249: 【97†now-reading-page】  | Generate a \"What I'm Reading\" webpage from your library — host it on your personal site\nL250: 【98†build-persona】  | Build a reading profile from your highlights, tags, and history — powers personalization across all other skills\nL251: ### Personalization\nL252: \nL253: Run the `build-persona` skill first to generate a `reader_persona.md` file. The other skills (triage, feed-catchup, quiz) read this file to personalize their output to your interests, goals, and reading style.\nL254: ## Please share yours!\nL255: \nL256: These skills are just a starting point, quickly hacked up by the Readwise team based on what's been for us to try. There is still so so much more that can be done. Please make a pull request adding your own favorite skills, or shoot us an email (hello@readwise.io) at any time :)\nL257: ## About\nL258: \nL259: Agent skills for your Readwise and Reader data, powered by the Readwise MCP server/CLI. Triage your inbox, quiz yourself on what you've read, build a personalized now-reading page, and more.\nL260: \nL261: 【71†readwise.io/mcp†readwise.io】\nL262: \nL263: ### Resources\nL264: \nL265: 【72†Readme】\nL266: \nL267: 【73†Activity】\nL268: \nL269: 【74†Custom properties】\nL270: \nL271: ### Stars\nL272: \nL273: 325 stars\nL274: \nL275: ### Watchers\nL276: \nL277: 2 watching\nL278: \nL279: ### Forks\nL280: \nL281: 【75†13 forks】\nL282: \nL283: 【76†Report repository】\nL284: \nL285: ## Releases\nL286: \nL287: ## Packages\nL288: \nL289: ## Contributors\nL290: \nL291: ## Languages\nL292: \nL293: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReadwise MCP Server - Readwise Docs (https://docs.readwise.io/tools/mcp)\nciteturn1020view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://docs.readwise.io/tools/mcp\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 265\nL0: Home\nL1: \nL2: Search docs\nL3: \nL4:   * 【0†Get Started】\nL5:   * 【1†Account FAQs】\nL6:   * 【2†Changelog】\nL7:   * 【3†Blog†blog.readwise.io】\nL8:   * Email Us (hello@readwise.io)\nL9:   * 【4†Affiliate Program】\nL10:   * 【5†MCP & CLI Tools】\nL11: \nL12:   * ## MCP & CLI Tools\nL13: \nL14:     * 【5†Overview】\nL15:     * 【6†MCP Setup】\nL16:     * 【7†CLI Setup】\nL17:     * 【8†Usage Examples】\nL18: \nL19:   1. 【0†Home】\nL20: \nL21:   2. 【5†Tools】\nL22: \nL23:   3. 【6†Mcp】\nL24: # Readwise MCP Server\nL25: \nL26: Get started at readwise.io/mcp\nL27: \nL28: These docs offer detailed instructions and FAQs about the Readwise MCP, but if you're just looking for a quick setup guide to get up and running, check out our landing page at 【9†readwise.io/mcp†readwise.io】.\nL29: ## What is the Readwise MCP?\nL30: \nL31: The 【10†Model Context Protocol (MCP)†modelcontextprotocol.io】 standardizes how applications provide context to Large Language Models (LLMs). The Readwise MCP was created to act as a bridge between LLM clients and Readwise.\nL32: The Readwise MCP server gives Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, or any MCP-compatible AI direct access to your Readwise highlights and Reader documents. Once connected, you can ask your AI to search your notes, answer questions using your own reading history as context, or even make changes to your Reader library for you.\nL33: ## Connecting your AI app\nL34: \nL35: The setup steps vary by app. Find your app below for step-by-step instructions.\nL36: \nL37: ## 【11†Claude Desktop】\nL38: \nL39: ## 【12†Claude Code】\nL40: \nL41: ## 【13†ChatGPT】\nL42: \nL43: ## 【14†Codex】\nL44: \nL45: ## 【15†Codex CLI】\nL46: \nL47: ## 【16†Cursor】\nL48: \nL49: ## 【17†OpenClaw】\nL50: \nL51: ## 【18†Perplexity】\nL52: \nL53: ## 【19†Other apps】\nL54: ### Claude Desktop (Chat & Cowork)\nL55: \nL56:   1. Open Customize (from the top left) and select Connectors.\nL57: 【20†Image: Connectors settings in Claude desktop app.】\nL58: \nL59:   2. Click the plus icon in the top right, then select Add custom connector.\nL60: 【21†Image: Add custom connector in Claude desktop app.】\nL61: \nL62:   3. Enter Readwise as the name and add the URL: `https://mcp2.readwise.io/mcp`\nL63: 【22†Image: Custom connector settings in Claude desktop app.】\nL64:   4. Click Add. Find the new connection in the list and use the Connect button to authorize with your Readwise account.\nL65: 【23†Image: Authorize Readwise connection in Claude desktop app.】\nL66: ### Claude Code\nL67: \nL68: Run this command in your terminal:\nL69: \nL70:     claude mcp add --transport http readwise https://mcp2.readwise.io/mcp\nL71: \nL72: \nL73: [Button: Copy]\nL74: \nL75: Then start Claude Code and run `/mcp`, select readwise, and select Authenticate.\nL76: ### ChatGPT\nL77: \nL78: Readwise is an 【24†official App within ChatGPT†chatgpt.com】. To find it, click into Apps in the sidebar.\nL79: \nL80: 【25†Image: ChatGPT Apps in sidebar.】\nL81: \nL82: Search for \"Readwise\", then click into the option that appears.\nL83: \nL84: 【26†Image: Search for the Readwise app in ChatGPT.】\nL85: \nL86: Click Connect. This will open a browser window for you to authorize the connection with your Readwise account.\nL87: \nL88: 【27†Image: Connect to the Readwise app in ChatGPT.】\nL89: ### Codex\nL90: \nL91: Readwise is an official App within Codex. To find it, click into Plugins in the sidebar.\nL92: \nL93: 【28†Image: Codex Plugins in sidebar.】\nL94: \nL95: Search for \"Readwise\", then click into the option that appears.\nL96: \nL97: 【29†Image: Search for the Readwise plugin in Codex.】\nL98: \nL99: Click the Add to Codex button in the top right corner.\nL100: \nL101: 【30†Image: Add the Readwise plugin in Codex.】\nL102: In the popup that appears, click the Install button to connect to your Readwise account. This will open a browser window to authorize Codex to access your Readwise data.\nL103: \nL104: 【31†Image: Install and authorize the Readwise plugin in Codex.】\nL105: ### Codex CLI\nL106: \nL107: Run this command in your terminal:\nL108: \nL109:     codex mcp add readwise --url https://mcp2.readwise.io/mcp\nL110: \nL111: \nL112: [Button: Copy]\nL113: \nL114: Log in to authenticate:\nL115: \nL116:     codex mcp login readwise\nL117: \nL118: \nL119: [Button: Copy]\nL120: \nL121: Start `codex` — it will have access to all of your Readwise data.\nL122: \nL123: ### Cursor\nL124: \nL125:   1. Click this button to open Cursor and add the Readwise MCP:\nL126: \nL127:   * Add to Cursor\nL128: \nL129:   2. Click Install to confirm.\nL130: ### OpenClaw\nL131: \nL132: For the best experience with OpenClaw, use the 【7†Readwise CLI】 instead. Have your claw run:\nL133: \nL134:     npm i -g @readwise/cli\nL135: \nL136: \nL137: [Button: Copy]\nL138: \nL139: The CLI works optimally with OpenClaw and will handle authentication and data access automatically.\nL140: ### Perplexity\nL141: \nL142: At this time, only Perplexity users with the Pro plan or higher have access to the custom MCP functionality. This feature is not currently available for users with free accounts.\nL143: \nL144: Click the Customize option in the left sidebar.\nL145: \nL146: 【32†Image: Perplexity Customize menu option.】\nL147: \nL148: On the following page, click Custom connector in the top right corner.\nL149: \nL150: 【33†Image: Perplexity custom connector button.】\nL151: \nL152: Fill out the form with the following information:\nL153: 【34†Image: Perplexity new connector creation form.】\nL154: \nL155:   * Icon: (optional) Upload an image to represent the connection. We've made one with the Readwise logo that you can download here, to make the connection look properly official.\nL156: 【35†Download Readwise icon】\nL157:   * Name: This can be whatever you'd like to use to find the connection in the list. We recommend \"Readwise\" or \"Readwise MCP\" to keep things simple.\nL158:   * Description: (optional) You can leave this blank, or you can enter something like \"Search Readwise highlights and Reader documents.\"\nL159:   * MCP Server URL: `https://mcp2.readwise.io/mcp`\nL160:   * I understand custom connectors can introduce risks: Check this box. (We promise we won't steal your data!)\nL161: Once you click Add, you'll be briefly redirected to the Readwise website to authenticate the connection. Click Authorize to continue.\nL162: ### Other apps\nL163: \nL164: For any apps that support adding MCPs as remote servers, use this URL to add the MCP directly:\nL165: \nL166:     https://mcp2.readwise.io/mcp\nL167: \nL168: \nL169: [Button: Copy]\nL170: \nL171: If your AI app doesn't support remote HTTP MCP servers, you can try adding it as a stdio server instead:\nL172: \nL173:     npx -y mcp-remote https://mcp2.readwise.io/mcp\nL174: \nL175: \nL176: [Button: Copy]\nL177: ## What you can do with the Readwise MCP\nL178: \nL179: Once connected, your AI tool can search across your highlights, notes, and saved Reader documents. Search combines full-text matching with semantic search, so it can surface relevant content even when your query doesn't use the exact words from your saves.\nL180: \nL181: You can also use the MCP to take actions on your Reader documents, like moving them to the archive or adding tags, or create new highlights in your Readwise library.\nL182: These are the actions available to your AI tool when using the Readwise MCP:\nL183: ### Reader MCP tools\nL184:   * Export your documents\nL185:   * Get the details and metadata of a document\nL186:   * Get all the highlights in a document\nL187:   * Get the status of a document export\nL188:   * List all of the documents currently in your account\nL189:   * List all of the tags you've created\nL190:   * Search all of your documents\nL191:   * Add tags to a document\nL192:   * Add tags to a highlight\nL193:   * Bulk edit document metadata\nL194:   * Create a new document\nL195:   * Create a new highlight\nL196:   * Move documents from one location to another (e.g. inbox, archive, shortlist)\nL197:   * Remove tags from a document\nL198:   * Remove tags from a highlight\nL199:   * Add a highlight note\nL200: ### Readwise MCP tools\nL201: \nL202:   * Get today's Daily Review\nL203:   * List all of your Readwise highlights\nL204:   * Search all of your Readwise highlights\nL205:   * Create a new highlight\nL206:   * Delete a highlight\nL207:   * Update an existing highlight\nL208: \nL209: Looking for inspiration?\nL210: \nL211: For more ideas about what you can do with these tools, check out our 【8†usage examples】 or 【36†browse pre-built skills on GitHub†github.com】.\nL212: \nL213: ## MCP FAQs\nL214: ### Does this access my Reader documents or just my Readwise highlights?\nL215: \nL216: Both. The integration indexes your Readwise highlights and Reader documents, making all of them available to your connected AI apps.\nL217: \nL218: ### How often does the index update?\nL219: \nL220: The index updates automatically as you add or update content. After the initial full index, subsequent syncs only process new or changed content, so they run quickly in the background.\nL221: ### Can I connect multiple AI apps at the same time?\nL222: \nL223: Yes. You can use the same MCP server URL with as many compatible apps as you like.\nL224: \nL225: ### Is this related to the older Readwise MCP server?\nL226: \nL227: The previous Readwise-only MCP server is being deprecated in favor of this one. The new server covers both Readwise and Reader data. If you configured the old server previously, you'll want to update your AI app to use the new MCP server URL instead by following the instructions above.\nL228: ## Questions?\nL229: \nL230: 【37†Image: Readwise Contact Us】\nL231: \nL232:   * Email Us hello@readwise.io\nL233:   * 【38†Follow Us@readwise†x.com】\nL234:   * 【39†Ask the Community Join us on Reddit†www.reddit.com】\nL235: \nL236: ## Have a suggestion?\nL237: \nL238: We're pretty familiar with our product, so we occasionally fall victim to the 【40†Curse of Knowledge†en.wikipedia.org】. If any part of this documentation confuses you or seems incomplete, please let us know!\nL239: \nL240: Send Feedback (hello@readwise.io)\nL241: ## On this page\nL242: \nL243:   1. ### 【41†What is the Readwise MCP?】\nL244: \nL245:   2. ### 【42†Connecting your AI app】\nL246: \nL247:     1. 【11†Claude Desktop (Chat & Cowork)】\nL248:     2. 【12†Claude Code】\nL249:     3. 【13†ChatGPT】\nL250:     4. 【14†Codex】\nL251:     5. 【15†Codex CLI】\nL252:     6. 【16†Cursor】\nL253:     7. 【17†OpenClaw】\nL254:     8. 【18†Perplexity】\nL255:     9. 【19†Other apps】\nL256:   3. ### 【43†What you can do with the Readwise MCP】\nL257: \nL258:     1. 【44†Reader MCP tools】\nL259:     2. 【45†Readwise MCP tools】\nL260:   4. ### 【46†MCP FAQs】\nL261:     1. 【47†Does this access my Reader documents or just my Readwise highlights?】\nL262:     2. 【48†How often does the index update?】\nL263:     3. 【49†Can I connect multiple AI apps at the same time?】\nL264:     4. 【50†Is this related to the older Readwise MCP server?】\n"
